{"id": "85831", "name": "שברים חלקיים ואינטגרל – x⁴(1−x)⁴/(1+x²), 3 סעיפים (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-left:8px;margin-right:8px\">a</span></div><p>Write the following in partial fractions.</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}} \\]</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:prt1]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-left:8px;margin-right:8px\">b</span></div><p>Integrate your expression with respect to \\(x\\).</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans2]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans2]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:prt2]]</div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"font-weight:bold;color:#4b1f6f;margin-bottom:8px\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:26px;height:26px;line-height:26px;text-align:center;border-radius:50%;background:#4b1f6f;color:#fff;margin-left:8px;margin-right:8px\">c</span></div><p>Find</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\int_{0}^{1} {{CT:0}} \\mathrm{d}x. \\]</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans3]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans3]]</div><div style=\"margin-top:6px\">[[feedback:prt3]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> The numerator has degree 8 and the denominator degree 2, so we first divide the polynomials. The remainder over the irreducible factor \\(1+x^2\\) is already a partial fraction (part a). Then we integrate term by term (part b) and substitute the limits (part c).</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Expanding the numerator</b><br>By the binomial formula \\((1-x)^4=1-4x+6x^2-4x^3+x^4\\), so<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ x^4(1-x)^4={{CT:1}} \\]</p>Its degree (8) is larger than the degree of \\(1+x^2\\) (2), so polynomial division comes first.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Polynomial long division by \\(x^2+1\\)</b><br>At each step we divide the leading term of what is left by \\(x^2\\), multiply the result by \\(x^2+1\\) and subtract:<table dir=\"ltr\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px auto\"><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\"><b>next term of the quotient</b></td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\"><b>term \\(\\times (x^2+1)\\)</b></td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\"><b>what is left</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:2}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:3}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:4}}\\)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:5}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:6}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:7}}\\)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:8}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:9}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:10}}\\)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:11}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:12}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:13}}\\)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:14}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:15}}\\)</td><td style=\"padding:2px 10px\">\\({{CT:16}}\\)</td></tr></table>The quotient is the sum of the terms in the first column and the remainder is the last number:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:1}}=\\left(x^2+1\\right)\\left({{CT:17}}\\right)+\\left({{CT:18}}\\right) \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 3 — The partial fractions (part a)</b><br>Dividing by \\(1+x^2\\), and since \\(1+x^2\\) has no real roots (it is an irreducible quadratic factor, and the remainder is a constant), there is nothing more to split:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}={{CT:19}} \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 4 — Integrating (part b)</b><br>We integrate term by term with \\(\\int x^n\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}\\) and \\(\\int \\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\tan^{-1} x\\) (the inverse tangent, also written \\(\\arctan x\\)):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\int {{CT:0}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x={{CT:20}}+c \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 5 — The definite integral (part c)</b><br>Write \\(F(x)={{CT:20}}\\). Then \\(F(0)={{CT:21}}\\), and since \\(\\tan^{-1} 1=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\),<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ F(1)={{CT:22}}+\\left({{CT:23}}\\right)+{{CT:24}}+\\left({{CT:25}}\\right)+{{CT:26}}-4\\tan^{-1}1={{CT:27}}-4\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{4}={{CT:28}} \\]</p>so that<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\int_{0}^{1} {{CT:0}}\\, \\mathrm{d}x = {{CT:28}} \\]</p>(The integrand is positive on \\((0,1)\\), so this shows \\(\\pi &lt; \\frac{22}{7}\\).)</div></div>", "specificfeedback": "", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "partfrac", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "int", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "int", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "PartFrac", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "p1", "testoptions": "x", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part a — incorrect.</b></div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "Int", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "p2", "testoptions": "x", "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part b — incorrect.</b></div>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans3", "tans": "p3", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "prt3-0-T", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-0-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part c — incorrect.</b></div>"}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "EqualComAss", "sans": "ans3", "tans": "p3", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-T", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part c — correct.</b></div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-F", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\"><b>Part c — incorrect.</b> Your value is equal to the right one, but it is not fully simplified. Please fully simplify your answer and write it in traditional form.</div>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["bestlength", "p", "p1", "p2", "p3", "pfC", "pfN", "pfP", "pfP1", "pfQ", "pfR", "pfS", "trylength"], "nvariants": 1}